<title>USA: St Paul hogs up $0.50 - USDA.</title>
<headline>St Paul hogs up $0.50 - USDA.</headline>
<dateline>ST PAUL 1997-01-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>USDA said barrows and gilts compared with Friday, trading was moderate, prices were $0.50 higher in a light test due to weekend weather conditions. Top $53.00 per cwt.</p>
<p>    US 1-3     220-250 lbs     53.00</p>
<p>		   250-260 lbs     52.50-53.00</p>
<p>		   260-270 lbs     51.50-52.50</p>
<p>    US 2-3     270-280 lbs     50.50-51.50</p>
<p>    US 2-4     280-290 lbs     49.50-50.50</p>
<p>Sows - steady to weak in light test. Top $53.00.</p>
<p>    US 1-3     300-400 lbs     44.00</p>
<p>		   400-550 lbs     Scarce</p>
<p>		   550-700 lbs     53.00</p>
</text>
